# Optional overrides — unifi-network-mcp has no required env vars.
# Authentication is per-request via headers (provided by the MCP caller).
# X-Unifi-Api-Key is always required, plus exactly ONE of X-Unifi-Host or
# X-Unifi-Console-Id, depending on which mode the console needs:
#
#   X-Unifi-Host         DIRECT MODE. The customer's self-hosted UniFi
#                        controller host, reachable from wherever this
#                        server runs — bare host/IP or a full https:// URL,
#                        with or without a port (normalized internally).
#                        IMPORTANT: this server calls the controller
#                        directly, so it only works if the controller is
#                        reachable from here — for a cloud-hosted gateway
#                        that means the customer has exposed their local
#                        controller's API to the internet (their own
#                        choice/risk — see README). Only exists for
#                        self-hosted/hardware consoles.
#
#   X-Unifi-Console-Id   CONNECTOR MODE (use for Official UniFi Hosting /
#                        SaaS, or any console the customer won't expose).
#                        The console's Site Manager host ID — find it with
#                        unifi_list_hosts. Requests go through Ubiquiti's
#                        own cloud (api.ui.com), never touching the
#                        customer's network at all.
#
#   X-Unifi-Api-Key      Always required, but a DIFFERENT KIND of key
#                        depending on mode:
#                          - direct mode: a LOCAL API key generated on the
#                            console itself (Settings > Control Plane >
#                            Integrations > API Keys).
#                          - connector mode: a SITE MANAGER API key
#                            generated at unifi.ui.com > Settings > API Keys.
#                        These are not interchangeable. Do not use the
#                        customer's admin username/password in either case.
#
#   X-Unifi-Verify-Ssl   Optional, defaults to "true". DIRECT MODE ONLY —
#                        ignored in connector mode (api.ui.com always has a
#                        real CA-signed cert). Set to "false" only if the
#                        console presents a self-signed certificate —
#                        discouraged, since the request is now going over
#                        the public internet (not a LAN), so skipping TLS
#                        verification has real MITM exposure. Prefer putting
#                        a valid cert on whatever the customer exposes
#                        instead.
#
# This server calls the Network Integration API directly with these
# per-request credentials — it has no shared/brokerable auth layer to
# delegate to a gateway, and never persists credentials beyond one request.

MCP_HTTP_PORT=8080
MCP_HTTP_HOST=0.0.0.0
